<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 148 0 R
/T (Our annual Women in Science STEMposium at Western University was an inspiring day filled with a ton of insight into the science world, and connections with our community. Students had the opportunity to engage in hands on activities, connect with women in STEM, and learn more about the diverse science pathways available at Western.  We would like to thank our incredible panel featuring Jennifer Evans, Mo Hagan, Sarah Gallagher with a keynote speaker Matt Davison, the Dean of the Faculty of Science. Each speaker shared valuable insights about their career journeys, challenges, and advice for students interested in pursuing STEM fields. We were also excited to have several other science clubs in attendance to share their clubs initiatives and goals in science. Thank you to everyone who attended, volunteered, and contributed to making STEMposium such a success. We loved seeing so many future scientists come together for a day of learning and inspiration.  We can't wait to do it again next year!)
/E (Our annual Women in Science STEMposium at Western University was an inspiring day filled with a ton of insight into the science world, and connections with our community. Students had the opportunity to engage in hands on activities, connect with women in STEM, and learn more about the diverse science pathways available at Western.  We would like to thank our incredible panel featuring Jennifer Evans, Mo Hagan, Sarah Gallagher with a keynote speaker Matt Davison, the Dean of the Faculty of Science. Each speaker shared valuable insights about their career journeys, challenges, and advice for students interested in pursuing STEM fields. We were also excited to have several other science clubs in attendance to share their clubs initiatives and goals in science. Thank you to everyone who attended, volunteered, and contributed to making STEMposium such a success. We loved seeing so many future scientists come together for a day of learning and inspiration.  We can't wait to do it again next year!)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
